From 100ca63a92f73741d2c11e726c811a84e5b1bfc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:59:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ARM64: let config.guess recognise aarch64 Cygwin/MSYS
 hosts

On a native Windows ARM64 Cygwin host, uname -s is CYGWIN_NT-*-ARM64 and
uname -m is aarch64.  This 2021 config.guess only knows the i686 and
x86_64 Cygwin hosts, so configure without --build failed with "unable to
guess system type".  Add the case that upstream config.guess has had
since 2023.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
 config/config.guess | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/config/config.guess b/config/config.guess
index e81d3ae..6e29f97 100644
--- a/config/config.guess
+++ b/config/config.guess
@@ -947,6 +947,9 @@ EOF
     amd64:CYGWIN*:*:* | x86_64:CYGWIN*:*:*)
 	GUESS=x86_64-pc-cygwin
 	;;
+    aarch64:CYGWIN*:*:*)
+	GUESS=aarch64-pc-cygwin
+	;;
     prep*:SunOS:5.*:*)
 	SUN_REL=`echo "$UNAME_RELEASE" | sed -e 's/[^.]*//'`
 	GUESS=powerpcle-unknown-solaris2$SUN_REL
-- 
2.56.1

